ces to high tech which  will potentially be important in China's  competition with the United States Xi  Jinping also made it clear that his goal  is to restore China to its rightful  historical place which means we will  probably see more assertiveness on the  international stage especially when it  comes to comfort confrontation with the  West  he spoke about high winds choppy Waters  and dangerous storms ahead what will be  the biggest challenges you'll have to  face  the greatest challenge that Xi Jinping  is likely to face is China's economy  which is not in a very great shape now  China's GDP growth has stalled or  considerably slowed down China's  unemployment is high and China's  property Market is in this slump also  covet lockdowns have caused many public  dissensifications and I think another  potential challenge is succession  there's a lot of uncertainty over when  or if Xi Jinping might eventually retire  or is he actually going to be leader for  life and I think any uncertainty over  successor can potentially so instability  or even lead to a succession Strife  further down the road are there any  likely successors that we might see  popping up this week  not this time I don't see any uh any  reason for Xi Jinping to make himself a  lane duck this time around if there's  any successor in his mind probably next  round we will see more clear signals  what can he do to turn the economy  around  so that's a great question I want to  make clear that China's economic rules  is a combination or mixture of  structural slowdown and XI jinping's own  policy missteps in the past few years  concretely some sort of facing out from  Draconian zero covet restrictions is a  must that might take some time but  ultimately it's gonna happen other  things are more complicated for example  some of XI jinping's policy initiatives  are correct at least in Direction  China's reduction of debt from its  Financial system redistribution of  wealth are written in of property Market  speculations  poverty reduction property Market  cleanup are all meritable in spirit but  the problem is the scale of those  regulatory storms have been too big and  China has relied too much on its state  sector at the expense of private ones so  some kind of course correction some kind  of returning to opening up and reform is  called for but we can't really expect  him to change course drastically from  here on out can we what is the rest of  the party think about that do they as he  demands think in one mind or is there  opposition  so as you know rumors of infighting and  power struggles are a fixture of Chinese  Elite politics especially in the lead up  to important events like the 20s party  in Congress but I think in the past  decade what Xi Jinping has successfully  done is to clean up the party  infrastructure under Xi Jinping people  who are loyal to him are more likely to  be promoted and this time around it's no  exception that means voice of descent  has considerably quieted down during the  the past few years the power of party  factions and Elders have also been  significantly weakened through teaching  teams into a corruption corruption  campaign so there are people who might  not be satisfied with XI jinping's  approach but I don't see them forming  meaningful coalition to pose a  meaningful challenge to XI Jin King's  World  Xi Jinping has used the Taiwan issue  many times to strengthen his his  position and his remarks on  reunification with the island actually  prompted the most euphoric response on  Sunday is that something he will  actively pursue in his third term  that's a great question there's actually  not much new information on Taiwan  coming out of the the National Congress  Beach made by Xi Jinping this past  weekend Xi Jinping repeats that Beijing  will resort to Peaceful means if  possible but he will not promise to  renounce the use of force and Xi Jinping  also emphasizes that complete  reunification of China our motherland i